IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`

§ `Chapter 2 -- General explanations: the defined terms`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 6A, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 17, 19, 20, 21, 22, 22A,
-- 27, 28, 29, 29A, 29B, 30, 31, 31A, 40, 41, 42, 43, 44, 44A, 45, 46, 47, 48,
-- 49, 50, 51.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The fault-element explanations (ss 23 to 26H) are in chapter-2-explanations.l4;
-- the attribution rules (ss 32 to 38) are in chapter-2-participation.l4.
--
-- Sections 13 to 16, 18, 39 and 52 do not exist or are repealed.

§§ `Section 6A -- Reach of the Chapter 2 definitions`

-- Every definition explained in ss 22A to 26H (except "dishonestly" in s 24 and
-- "fraudulently" in s 25) applies to any offence in this Code OR in any other
-- written law, unless that other written law expressly defines the same word.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 6A"
DECLARE `Definition Reach Facts` HAS
    `the term is explained in sections 22A to 26H` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term is dishonestly as explained in section 24` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term is fraudulently as explained in section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is in this Code` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other written law expressly provides its own definition or explanation of the same term` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 6A"
@export Decide whether a Penal Code 1871 Chapter 2 explanation carries across to an offence in another written law
GIVEN d IS A `Definition Reach Facts` @desc The term and the offence it is to be applied to. ss 24 and 25 are carved out of the carry-across, and any express definition in the other written law displaces the Code explanation.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 22A to 26H explanation applies to the offence` IF
        d's `the term is explained in sections 22A to 26H`
    AND (NOT d's `the term is dishonestly as explained in section 24`)
    AND (NOT d's `the term is fraudulently as explained in section 25`)
    AND (   d's `the offence is in this Code`
         OR (NOT d's `the other written law expressly provides its own definition or explanation of the same term`))

§§ `Section 7 -- An expression once explained keeps its sense`

-- s 7 is a rule of construction addressed to the reader of the Code, not a test
-- over facts: every expression explained in any part of the Code is used in every
-- part in conformity with the explanation. It is honoured here by the encoding's
-- own discipline -- each explained term has exactly one definition module and
-- every offence module imports it rather than restating it. Nothing to decide.

§§ `Sections 8, 9, 10 -- Gender, number, man and woman`

-- s 8: the pronoun "he" and its derivatives are used of any person, whether male
-- or female. s 9: unless the contrary appears from the context, the singular
-- includes the plural and the plural the singular. Both are drafting conventions
-- with no factual test; this encoding writes gender-neutrally throughout.
-- s 10: "man" denotes a male human being of any age; "woman" a female human being
-- of any age. Age is irrelevant to both.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 10"
DECLARE Sex IS ONE OF
    `man`
    `woman`

§§ `Section 11 -- Person`

-- "Person" includes any company or association or body of persons, whether
-- incorporated or not. This matters to s 415 Explanations 4 and 5, which let a
-- company be deceived or induced with no individual officer personally deceived.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 11"
DECLARE `Person Kind` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company`
    `an association or body of persons whether incorporated or not`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 11"
@export Decide whether something is a person within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 11
GIVEN k IS A `Person Kind` @desc An individual, a company, or an association or body of persons whether incorporated or not. All three are persons for the Code.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a person within section 11` k IS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a company` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an association or body of persons whether incorporated or not` THEN TRUE

§§ `Section 12 -- Public`

-- "Public" includes any class of the public or any community.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 12"
DECLARE `Public Facts` HAS
    `the group is the public at large` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the group is a class of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the group is a community` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 12"
GIVEN p IS A `Public Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the group is the public within section 12` IF
        p's `the group is the public at large`
    OR  p's `the group is a class of the public`
    OR  p's `the group is a community`

§§ `Section 17 -- Government`

-- "Government" includes any person lawfully performing executive functions of the
-- Government under any law.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 17"
DECLARE `Government Facts` HAS
    `is the Government itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a person lawfully performing executive functions of the Government under any law` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 17"
GIVEN g IS A `Government Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Government within section 17` IF
        g's `is the Government itself`
    OR  g's `is a person lawfully performing executive functions of the Government under any law`

§§ `Section 19 -- Judge`

-- "Judge" denotes not only every person officially designated as a judge, but also
-- every person empowered by law to give, in any legal proceeding civil or criminal,
-- a definitive judgment, or a judgment which if not appealed against would be
-- definitive, or a judgment which if confirmed by some other authority would be
-- definitive, or who is one of a body of persons so empowered.
-- Illustration (c): a Magistrate who can only commit for trial is not a judge.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 19"
DECLARE `Judicial Office Facts` HAS
    `is officially designated as a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if not appealed against would be definitive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if confirmed by another authority would be definitive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is empowered only to commit for trial to another court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is empowered by law to act judicially alone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 19"
@export Decide whether a person is a judge within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 19
GIVEN j IS A `Judicial Office Facts` @desc Official designation, or a power to give a definitive judgment (or one definitive if not appealed against, or if confirmed by another authority), or membership of a body so empowered. A power only to commit for trial to another court is not enough (Illustration (c)).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a judge within section 19` IF
        j's `is officially designated as a judge`
    OR  j's `is empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding`
    OR  j's `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if not appealed against would be definitive`
    OR  j's `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if confirmed by another authority would be definitive`
    OR  j's `is one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment`

§§ `Section 20 -- Court of justice`

-- "Court of justice" denotes a judge empowered by law to act judicially alone, or a
-- body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body, when that judge or
-- body is acting judicially.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 20"
@export Decide whether something is a court of justice within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 20
GIVEN j IS A `Judicial Office Facts` @desc A judge (s 19) empowered to act judicially alone, or a body of judges empowered to act judicially as a body, in either case while actually acting judicially.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a court of justice within section 20` IF
        (   (    `is a judge within section 19` j
             AND j's `is empowered by law to act judicially alone`)
         OR j's `is a body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body`)
    AND j's `is acting judicially`

§§ `Section 21 -- Public servant`

-- s 21(1)(a) to (j). Explanation 1: it is immaterial whether the person was
-- appointed by the Government. Explanation 2: a person in actual possession of the
-- situation of a public servant is a public servant whatever the legal defect in
-- his right to hold it.
-- s 21(2): in ss 175, 178, 179, 180 and 228, "public servant" excludes a judge as
-- defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 21(1)"
DECLARE `Public Servant Facts` HAS
    `is an officer in the Singapore Armed Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an officer of a court of justice with a duty of the kind in paragraph c` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an arbitrator or other person to whom a matter has been referred for decision or report` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of the kind in paragraph g` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an officer with a duty touching Government property revenue or pecuniary interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in the service or pay of Government or remunerated by fees or commission for a public duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a member of the Public Service Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is employed to carry out paragraph g duties on behalf of the Government or a statutory body and is performing them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in actual possession of the situation of a public servant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the charge is under section 175 178 179 180 or 228` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice Protection Act 2016` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 21(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Public Servant Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls within a description in section 21(1)` IF
        p's `is an officer in the Singapore Armed Forces`
    OR  p's `is a judge`
    OR  p's `is an officer of a court of justice with a duty of the kind in paragraph c`
    OR  p's `is an assessor assisting a court of justice or public servant`
    OR  p's `is an arbitrator or other person to whom a matter has been referred for decision or report`
    OR  p's `holds an office empowering him to place or keep a person in confinement`
    OR  p's `is an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of the kind in paragraph g`
    OR  p's `is an officer with a duty touching Government property revenue or pecuniary interests`
    OR  p's `is in the service or pay of Government or remunerated by fees or commission for a public duty`
    OR  p's `is a member of the Public Service Judicial Service or Legal Service Commission`
    OR  p's `is employed to carry out paragraph g duties on behalf of the Government or a statutory body and is performing them`

-- Explanation 2 makes actual possession of the situation sufficient, whatever the
-- defect in the right to hold it, so it is a further disjunct and not a proviso.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 21"
@export Decide whether a person is a public servant within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 21
GIVEN p IS A `Public Servant Facts` @desc Any of the descriptions in s 21(1)(a) to (j), or actual possession of the situation of a public servant (Explanation 2). For a charge under s 175, 178, 179, 180 or 228, a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016 is excluded by s 21(2).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a public servant within section 21` IF
        (   `falls within a description in section 21(1)` p
         OR p's `is in actual possession of the situation of a public servant`)
    AND (NOT (    p's `the charge is under section 175 178 179 180 or 228`
              AND p's `is a judge as defined in the Administration of Justice Protection Act 2016`))

§§ `Section 22 -- Property`

-- "immovable property" means land, benefits to arise out of land and things
-- attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth.
-- "movable property" includes property of every description except immovable
-- property. "property" means money and all other property, movable or immovable,
-- including things in action, other intangible or incorporeal property and virtual
-- currency. "virtual currency" is a digital representation of value in money or
-- money's worth that can be digitally traded and functions as a medium of exchange,
-- a unit of account or a store of value, whether or not legal tender anywhere.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22"
DECLARE `Property Facts` HAS
    `is land or a benefit to arise out of land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a thing attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a thing in action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money worth that can be digitally traded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `functions as a medium of exchange a unit of account or a store of value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is some other property of any description` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22"
GIVEN p IS A `Property Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is virtual currency within section 22` IF
        p's `is a digital representation of value in money or money worth that can be digitally traded`
    AND p's `functions as a medium of exchange a unit of account or a store of value`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22"
GIVEN p IS A `Property Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is immovable property within section 22` IF
        p's `is land or a benefit to arise out of land`
    OR  p's `is a thing attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22"
@export Decide whether something is movable property within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 22
GIVEN p IS A `Property Facts` @desc Movable property is property of every description except immovable property. Money, things in action, other intangible or incorporeal property and virtual currency are all property, and none of them is immovable, so all are movable.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is movable property within section 22` IF
        `is property within section 22` p
    AND (NOT `is immovable property within section 22` p)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22"
@export Decide whether something is property within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 22
GIVEN p IS A `Property Facts` @desc Money and all other property, movable or immovable, including things in action, other intangible or incorporeal property and virtual currency.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is property within section 22` IF
        p's `is money`
    OR  p's `is a thing in action`
    OR  p's `is other intangible or incorporeal property`
    OR  `is virtual currency within section 22` p
    OR  `is immovable property within section 22` p
    OR  p's `is some other property of any description`

§§ `Section 22A -- Fault element and physical element`

-- s 22A(1): a fault element is any state of mind, proof of which is needed to
-- establish liability, including but not limited to intention, wilfulness,
-- knowledge, rashness and negligence.
-- s 22A(2): a physical element is any fact, proof of which is needed to establish
-- liability, that is not a fault element of that offence.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22A"
DECLARE `Element Facts` HAS
    `proof of it is needed to establish liability under the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a state of mind` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22A(1)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Element Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a fault element of the offence` IF
        e's `proof of it is needed to establish liability under the offence`
    AND e's `it is a state of mind`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 22A(2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Element Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a physical element of the offence` IF
        e's `proof of it is needed to establish liability under the offence`
    AND (NOT e's `it is a state of mind`)

§§ `Section 27 -- Property in the possession of a spouse, clerk or servant`

-- When property is in the possession of a person's spouse, clerk or servant, on
-- account of that person, it is in that person's possession within the meaning of
-- the Code. Explanation: a person employed temporarily or on a particular occasion
-- in the capacity of a clerk or servant is a clerk or servant for this section.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 27"
DECLARE `Possession Facts` HAS
    `the person has the property physically` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the property is in the possession of the person spouse clerk or servant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that holding is on account of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder is employed only temporarily or on a particular occasion as a clerk or servant` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 27"
@export Decide whether property is in a person possession within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 27
GIVEN p IS A `Possession Facts` @desc Possession by the person, or by that person spouse, clerk or servant on that person account. Temporary or occasional employment as a clerk or servant still counts (Explanation).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is in the person possession within section 27` IF
        p's `the person has the property physically`
    OR  (    p's `the property is in the possession of the person spouse clerk or servant`
         AND p's `that holding is on account of the person`)

§§ `Section 28 -- Counterfeit`

-- A person "counterfeits" who causes one thing to resemble another thing, intending
-- by means of that resemblance to practise deception, or knowing it to be likely
-- that deception will thereby be practised.
-- Explanation 1: the imitation need not be exact.
-- Explanation 2: where the resemblance is such that a person might be deceived, the
-- intention or knowledge is presumed until the contrary is proved.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 28"
DECLARE `Counterfeit Facts` HAS
    `causes one thing to resemble another thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the imitation is exact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends by means of that resemblance to practise deception` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows it to be likely that deception will thereby be practised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the resemblance is such that a person might be deceived by it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contrary of the presumed intention or knowledge is proved` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 28 Explanation 2"
GIVEN c IS A `Counterfeit Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 28 presumption supplies the fault element` IF
        c's `the resemblance is such that a person might be deceived by it`
    AND (NOT c's `the contrary of the presumed intention or knowledge is proved`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 28"
@export Decide whether a person counterfeits within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 28
GIVEN c IS A `Counterfeit Facts` @desc Causing one thing to resemble another with intent to practise deception by that resemblance, or knowing deception is likely. The imitation need not be exact (Explanation 1), and where the resemblance is such that a person might be deceived the fault element is presumed until the contrary is proved (Explanation 2).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counterfeits within section 28` IF
        c's `causes one thing to resemble another thing`
    AND (   c's `intends by means of that resemblance to practise deception`
         OR c's `knows it to be likely that deception will thereby be practised`
         OR `the section 28 presumption supplies the fault element` c)

§§ `Section 29 -- Document`

-- "Document" includes, in addition to a document in writing, (a) any map, plan,
-- graph or drawing; (b) any photograph; (c) any label, marking or other writing
-- identifying or describing anything of which it forms a part or to which it is
-- attached; (d) any disc, tape, soundtrack or other device embodying sounds or
-- other data (not visual images) capable of reproduction; (e) any film, negative,
-- tape, disc or other device embodying visual images capable of reproduction;
-- (f) any paper or other material bearing marks, impressions, figures, letters,
-- symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 29, 29A, 29B, 30, 31, 31A"
DECLARE `Document Facts` HAS
    `is a document in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a map plan graph or drawing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a photograph` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a label marking or other writing identifying or describing the thing it forms part of or is attached to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a device embodying sounds or other data not being visual images capable of reproduction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a device embodying one or more visual images capable of reproduction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is material bearing marks figures letters symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an electronic record within the Electronic Transactions Act 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
    `creates extends transfers restricts extinguishes or releases a legal right or acknowledges a legal liability or the absence of a legal right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purports to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a credit charge stored value or automated teller machine card or other card carrying money money worth or financial rights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a testamentary document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a plate type tool chop or implement or any part or stamp or impression of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a postage or revenue stamp a seal or a device on or in which information is recorded or stored` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 29"
@export Decide whether something is a document within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 29
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts` @desc A document in writing, or any of the six extended categories in s 29(a) to (f).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a document within section 29` IF
        d's `is a document in writing`
    OR  d's `is a map plan graph or drawing`
    OR  d's `is a photograph`
    OR  d's `is a label marking or other writing identifying or describing the thing it forms part of or is attached to`
    OR  d's `is a device embodying sounds or other data not being visual images capable of reproduction`
    OR  d's `is a device embodying one or more visual images capable of reproduction`
    OR  d's `is material bearing marks figures letters symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them`

§§ `Section 29A -- Writing`

-- "Writing" includes any mode of representing or reproducing words, figures,
-- drawings or symbols in a visible form. Encoded within `is a document in writing`
-- and `is material bearing marks ...`, which together carry the visible-form test.

§§ `Section 29B -- Electronic record`

-- "Electronic record" has the same meaning as in the Electronic Transactions
-- Act 2010. That Act is not in this source bundle, so the test is a caller-asserted
-- fact: `is an electronic record within the Electronic Transactions Act 2010`.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 29B"
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an electronic record within section 29B` IF
    d's `is an electronic record within the Electronic Transactions Act 2010`

§§ `Section 30 -- Valuable security`

-- s 30(1): a document or electronic record which is, or purports to be, one whereby
-- any legal right is created, extended, transferred, restricted, extinguished or
-- released, or whereby a person acknowledges that he lies under legal liability or
-- has not a certain legal right.
-- s 30(2): includes credit cards, charge cards, stored value cards, automated
-- teller machine cards and other cards with money, money's worth or financial
-- rights attached.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 30"
@export Decide whether something is a valuable security within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 30
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts` @desc A document or electronic record which is or purports to be one dealing with a legal right or acknowledging a legal liability, or a card of the kinds listed in s 30(2).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a valuable security within section 30` IF
        (    (   `is a document within section 29` d
              OR `is an electronic record within section 29B` d)
         AND (   d's `creates extends transfers restricts extinguishes or releases a legal right or acknowledges a legal liability or the absence of a legal right`
              OR d's `purports to do so`))
    OR  d's `is a credit charge stored value or automated teller machine card or other card carrying money money worth or financial rights`

§§ `Section 31 -- A will`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 31"
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a will within section 31` IF
    d's `is a testamentary document`

§§ `Section 31A -- Die and instrument`

-- For Chapters 12 and 18 only. "Die" includes any plate, type, tool, chop or
-- implement and any part of one, and any stamp or impression of one.
-- "Instrument" includes any document formal or informal, any postage or revenue
-- stamp, any seal or die, and any device on or in which information is recorded.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 31A"
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a die within section 31A` IF
    d's `is a plate type tool chop or implement or any part or stamp or impression of one`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 31A"
GIVEN d IS A `Document Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an instrument within section 31A` IF
        `is a document within section 29` d
    OR  d's `is a postage or revenue stamp a seal or a device on or in which information is recorded or stored`
    OR  `is a die within section 31A` d

§§ `Sections 40 and 41 -- Offence`

-- s 40(1): except in the Chapters and sections in (2) and (3), "offence" denotes a
-- thing made punishable by this Code.
-- s 40(2): in Chapters 4, 4A, 5 and 5A, and in ss 4, 187, 194, 195, 203, 204B, 211,
-- 213, 214, 221, 222, 223, 224, 225, 327, 328, 329, 330, 331, 347, 348, 388 and 389,
-- "offence" denotes a thing punishable under this Code OR under any other written
-- law in force.
-- s 40(3): in ss 141, 176, 177, 201, 202, 212, 216 and 441, "offence" has that wider
-- meaning only where the thing punishable under the other law is punishable with
-- imprisonment for a term of 6 months or upwards, with or without fine.
-- s 41: an offence described as punishable with imprisonment "for a specified term
-- or upwards" includes an offence for which the specified term is the maximum.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 40 and 41"
DECLARE `Offence Reference Facts` HAS
    `the thing is made punishable by this Code` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is punishable under some other written law in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maximum imprisonment under that other law in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the reference is in Chapter 4 4A 5 or 5A or in a section 40(2) section` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reference is in a section 40(3) section` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 40"
@export Decide whether something is an offence for the purposes of a given reference in Penal Code 1871 section 40
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence Reference Facts` @desc Where the word "offence" appears matters. In the general case it means a thing punishable by this Code. In Chapters 4, 4A, 5 and 5A and the s 40(2) sections it extends to any other written law. In the s 40(3) sections it extends to another written law only where that law prescribes imprisonment of 6 months or upwards.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence for this reference` IF
        o's `the thing is made punishable by this Code`
    OR  (    o's `the reference is in Chapter 4 4A 5 or 5A or in a section 40(2) section`
         AND o's `the thing is punishable under some other written law in force`)
    OR  (    o's `the reference is in a section 40(3) section`
         AND o's `the thing is punishable under some other written law in force`
         AND o's `the maximum imprisonment under that other law in months` AT LEAST 6)

§§ `Section 42 -- Obscene`

-- "Obscene", in relation to any thing or matter, means any thing or matter the
-- effect of which is, if taken as a whole, such as to tend to deprave and corrupt
-- persons who are likely, having regard to all relevant circumstances, to read, see
-- or hear the matter contained or embodied in it.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 42"
DECLARE `Obscenity Facts` HAS
    `taken as a whole its effect tends to deprave and corrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `those it tends to deprave and corrupt are persons likely in all the circumstances to read see or hear it` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 42"
@export Decide whether a thing or matter is obscene within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 42
GIVEN o IS AN `Obscenity Facts` @desc The test is on the thing taken as a whole, and is directed at the persons likely, in all the relevant circumstances, to read, see or hear it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is obscene within section 42` IF
        o's `taken as a whole its effect tends to deprave and corrupt`
    AND o's `those it tends to deprave and corrupt are persons likely in all the circumstances to read see or hear it`

§§ `Section 43 -- Illegal, unlawful and legally bound to do`

-- "Illegal" or "unlawful" applies to everything which is an offence, or which is
-- prohibited by law, or which furnishes ground for a civil action. A person is
-- "legally bound to do" whatever it is illegal or unlawful in him to omit.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 43"
DECLARE `Legality Facts` HAS
    `the thing is an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is prohibited by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing furnishes ground for a civil action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing in question is an omission` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 43"
@export Decide whether something is illegal or unlawful within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 43
GIVEN l IS A `Legality Facts` @desc An offence, or a thing prohibited by law, or a thing which furnishes ground for a civil action.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is illegal within section 43` IF
        l's `the thing is an offence`
    OR  l's `the thing is prohibited by law`
    OR  l's `the thing furnishes ground for a civil action`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 43"
@export Decide whether a person is legally bound to do something within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 43
GIVEN l IS A `Legality Facts` @desc A person is legally bound to do whatever it is illegal or unlawful in him to omit, so the facts describe the omission.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is legally bound to do the act within section 43` IF
        l's `the thing in question is an omission`
    AND `is illegal within section 43` l

§§ `Sections 44 and 44A -- Injury and bodily injury`

-- s 44: "injury" denotes any harm whatever illegally caused to any person, in body,
-- mind, reputation or property.
-- s 44A: "bodily injury" denotes a series of bodily injuries as well as a single one.
-- That singular-or-series extension is the whole of s 44A; the base sense (harm to
-- the body) comes from s 44, so both limbs appear below.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 44 and 44A"
DECLARE `Injury Facts` HAS
    `harm is caused to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm is illegally caused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm is to the body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm is to the mind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm is to reputation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm is to property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm is a series of bodily injuries rather than a single bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 44"
@export Decide whether there is an injury within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 44
GIVEN i IS AN `Injury Facts` @desc Any harm whatever illegally caused to any person in body, mind, reputation or property. A harm not illegally caused is not an injury.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an injury within section 44` IF
        i's `harm is caused to a person`
    AND i's `the harm is illegally caused`
    AND (   i's `the harm is to the body`
         OR i's `the harm is to the mind`
         OR i's `the harm is to reputation`
         OR i's `the harm is to property`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 44A"
GIVEN i IS AN `Injury Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a bodily injury within section 44A` IF
        `is an injury within section 44` i
    AND (   i's `the harm is to the body`
         OR i's `the harm is a series of bodily injuries rather than a single bodily injury`)

§§ `Sections 45, 46, 47, 48 -- Life, death, animal, vessel`

-- s 45: "life" denotes the life of a human being unless the contrary appears from
-- the context. s 46: "death" likewise denotes the death of a human being.
-- s 47: "animal" denotes any living creature other than a human being.
-- s 48: "vessel" denotes anything made for the conveyance by water of human beings
-- or of property.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 45, 46, 47, 48"
DECLARE `Subject Facts` HAS
    `is a human being` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a living creature` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made for the conveyance by water of human beings or of property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contrary intention appears from the context` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 45"
@export Decide whether a reference to life is the life of a human being under Penal Code 1871 section 45
GIVEN s IS A `Subject Facts` @desc "Life" denotes the life of a human being unless the contrary appears from the context.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the life of a human being within section 45` IF
        s's `is a human being`
    AND (NOT s's `a contrary intention appears from the context`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 46"
@export Decide whether a reference to death is the death of a human being under Penal Code 1871 section 46
GIVEN s IS A `Subject Facts` @desc "Death" denotes the death of a human being unless the contrary appears from the context.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the death of a human being within section 46` IF
        s's `is a human being`
    AND (NOT s's `a contrary intention appears from the context`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 47"
GIVEN s IS A `Subject Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an animal within section 47` IF
        s's `is a living creature`
    AND (NOT s's `is a human being`)

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 48"
GIVEN s IS A `Subject Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a vessel within section 48` IF
    s's `is made for the conveyance by water of human beings or of property`

§§ `Sections 49 and 50 -- Year, month, section`

-- s 49: a year or a month is reckoned according to the Gregorian calendar.
-- s 50: "section" denotes one of the portions of a Chapter distinguished by
-- prefixed numeral figures.
-- Both are conventions of reading with no factual test. Every period in this
-- encoding is a Gregorian year or month by construction.

§§ `Section 51 -- Oath`

-- "Oath" includes a solemn affirmation substituted by law for an oath, and any
-- declaration required or authorised by law to be made before a public servant, or
-- to be used for the purpose of proof, whether in a court of justice or not.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 51"
DECLARE `Oath Facts` HAS
    `is an oath in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a solemn affirmation substituted by law for an oath` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a declaration required or authorised by law to be made before a public servant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a declaration required or authorised by law to be used for the purpose of proof` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 51"
@export Decide whether something is an oath within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 51
GIVEN o IS AN `Oath Facts` @desc An oath, a solemn affirmation substituted by law for one, or a declaration required or authorised by law to be made before a public servant or used for the purpose of proof, in or out of a court of justice.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an oath within section 51` IF
        o's `is an oath in the ordinary sense`
    OR  o's `is a solemn affirmation substituted by law for an oath`
    OR  o's `is a declaration required or authorised by law to be made before a public servant`
    OR  o's `is a declaration required or authorised by law to be used for the purpose of proof`

§§ `Illustrations`

`a Magistrate who can only commit for trial` MEANS `Judicial Office Facts` WITH
    `is officially designated as a judge` IS FALSE
    `is empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS FALSE
    `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if not appealed against would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if confirmed by another authority would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `is one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS FALSE
    `is empowered only to commit for trial to another court` IS TRUE
    `is empowered by law to act judicially alone` IS TRUE
    `is a body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body` IS FALSE
    `is acting judicially` IS TRUE

`a Magistrate who may sentence` MEANS `Judicial Office Facts` WITH
    `is officially designated as a judge` IS FALSE
    `is empowered by law to give a definitive judgment in a legal proceeding` IS FALSE
    `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if not appealed against would be definitive` IS TRUE
    `is empowered by law to give a judgment which if confirmed by another authority would be definitive` IS FALSE
    `is one of a body of persons empowered by law to give such a judgment` IS FALSE
    `is empowered only to commit for trial to another court` IS FALSE
    `is empowered by law to act judicially alone` IS TRUE
    `is a body of judges empowered by law to act judicially as a body` IS FALSE
    `is acting judicially` IS TRUE

`a bitcoin holding` MEANS `Property Facts` WITH
    `is land or a benefit to arise out of land` IS FALSE
    `is a thing attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is money` IS FALSE
    `is a thing in action` IS FALSE
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS FALSE
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money worth that can be digitally traded` IS TRUE
    `functions as a medium of exchange a unit of account or a store of value` IS TRUE
    `is some other property of any description` IS FALSE

`a plot of land` MEANS `Property Facts` WITH
    `is land or a benefit to arise out of land` IS TRUE
    `is a thing attached to the earth or permanently fastened to anything attached to the earth` IS FALSE
    `is money` IS FALSE
    `is a thing in action` IS FALSE
    `is other intangible or incorporeal property` IS FALSE
    `is a digital representation of value in money or money worth that can be digitally traded` IS FALSE
    `functions as a medium of exchange a unit of account or a store of value` IS FALSE
    `is some other property of any description` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`is a judge within section 19` `a Magistrate who can only commit for trial`)
#ASSERT `is a judge within section 19` `a Magistrate who may sentence`
#ASSERT `is a court of justice within section 20` `a Magistrate who may sentence`
#ASSERT `is virtual currency within section 22` `a bitcoin holding`
#ASSERT `is movable property within section 22` `a bitcoin holding`
#ASSERT `is property within section 22` `a plot of land`
#ASSERT NOT (`is movable property within section 22` `a plot of land`)
#ASSERT `is a person within section 11` `a company`
